# Cursor Rules for Soundscape

## General Principles

- Prioritize simplicity, readability, and maintainability above all
- Write minimal, focused code without unnecessary abstractions
- Use TypeScript strictly - never use `any` without explicit justification
- Follow established patterns in the codebase
- Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility

## Code Style

### TypeScript

- Use explicit types for all function parameters and return values
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use `type` for unions, intersections, and primitives
- Always enable strict mode
- Use optional chaining (`?.`) and nullish coalescing (`??`)

```typescript
// ✅ Good
interface User {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  email?: string;
}

function getUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
  // ...
}

// ❌ Bad
function getUser(id) {
  // ...
}
```

### Naming Conventions

- **Files**: kebab-case (`user-profile.tsx`, `fetch-data.ts`)
- **Components**: PascalCase (`UserProfile`, `TrackList`)
- **Functions**: camelCase (`fetchRecentTracks`, `formatDate`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_RETRIES`)
- **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase (`User`, `RecentTracksResponse`)

## SolidJS Specific Rules

### Reactivity

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Access props directly
const Component: Component<Props> = (props) => {
  return <div>{props.value}</div>;
};

// ❌ Bad: Destructuring breaks reactivity
const Component: Component<Props> = ({ value }) => {
  return <div>{value}</div>;
};

// ✅ Good: Use getters for derived values
const doubled = () => props.value * 2;

// ❌ Bad: Computed values break reactivity
const doubled = props.value * 2;
```

### Signals and State

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Use createSignal for local state
const [count, setCount] = createSignal(0);

// ✅ Good: Use createMemo for expensive computations
const filtered = createMemo(() => items().filter(item => item.active));

// ✅ Good: Use createResource for async data
const [data] = createResource(userId, fetchUser);
```

### Control Flow

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Use SolidJS control flow components
<Show when={user()}>
  <div>{user()!.name}</div>
</Show>

<For each={items()}>
  {(item) => <div>{item.name}</div>}
</For>

// ❌ Bad: Don't use ternaries for conditional rendering
{user() ? <div>{user()!.name}</div> : null}

// ❌ Bad: Don't use .map() for lists
{items().map(item => <div>{item.name}</div>)}
```

## React (Extension Only)

- Extension popup uses React due to WXT requirements
- Use functional components with hooks
- Minimize state complexity in extension UI

```typescript
// ✅ Good
const Popup: React.FC = () => {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);
  return <div onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}>...</div>;
};
```

## Styling with Tailwind

### Use Design System Tokens

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Use design system colors
<div class='bg-bg text-fg border-border'>

// ❌ Bad: Arbitrary colors
<div class='bg-white text-black border-gray-200'>
```

### Compose Utilities

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Compose utilities inline
<div class='flex items-center gap-2 p-2 border-b border-border hover:bg-bg-subtle'>

// ✅ Good: Extract complex patterns to @layer components
// In globals.css
@layer components {
  .btn {
    @apply px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors rounded;
    @apply hover:bg-bg-muted focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-border-hover;
  }
}
```

### Responsive Design

- Design mobile-first
- Use responsive prefixes sparingly
- Keep layouts simple and adaptive

```typescript
// ✅ Good
<div class='grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-2'>
```

## Data Fetching & APIs

### Last.fm Integration

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Use shared utils
import { fetchRecentTracks } from '@soundscape/utils';

// ✅ Good: Handle errors explicitly
try {
  const data = await fetchRecentTracks(username, page);
  return data;
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Failed to fetch:', error);
  throw error;
}

// ❌ Bad: Direct fetch calls
const response = await fetch(`https://ws.audioscrobbler.com/...`);
```

### Resource Factories (SolidJS)

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Return computed accessors
export function createResource(username: () => string) {
  const [data] = createResource(username, fetchData);
  
  return {
    items: () => data()?.items || [],
    isLoading: () => data.loading,
    error: () => data.error,
  };
}

// ❌ Bad: Return raw resource
export function createResource(username: () => string) {
  return createResource(username, fetchData);
}
```

## Component Structure

### SolidJS Components

```typescript
import { Component, createSignal, Show, For } from 'solid-js';
import type { ItemType } from '@soundscape/types';

interface ComponentProps {
  items: ItemType[];
  onItemClick?: (item: ItemType) => void;
}

const MyComponent: Component<ComponentProps> = (props) => {
  // 1. Local state
  const [isExpanded, setIsExpanded] = createSignal(false);
  
  // 2. Derived values
  const itemCount = () => props.items.length;
  
  // 3. Event handlers
  const handleClick = (item: ItemType) => {
    props.onItemClick?.(item);
  };
  
  // 4. Render
  return (
    <div class='space-y-2'>
      <Show when={itemCount() > 0}>
        <For each={props.items}>
          {(item) => (
            <div onClick={() => handleClick(item)}>
              {item.name}
            </div>
          )}
        </For>
      </Show>
    </div>
  );
};

export default MyComponent;
```

## File Organization

### Import Order

```typescript
// 1. External dependencies
import { Component, createSignal } from 'solid-js';

// 2. Internal shared packages
import type { Track } from '@soundscape/types';
import { fetchTracks } from '@soundscape/utils';

// 3. Local imports
import TrackList from './components/TrackList';
import { formatDate } from './lib/utils';
```

### Export Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Named exports for utilities
export function formatDate(date: Date): string { }
export function parseDate(str: string): Date { }

// ✅ Good: Default export for components
const Component: Component = () => { };
export default Component;
```

## Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Specific error messages
if (!username?.trim()) {
  throw new Error('Username is required');
}

if (!response.ok) {
  throw new Error(`Failed to fetch: ${response.statusText}`);
}

// ✅ Good: Let errors propagate to UI error boundaries
const [data] = createResource(fetchData); // Automatically handles errors

// ❌ Bad: Silent failures
try {
  await doSomething();
} catch {
  // nothing
}

// ❌ Bad: Generic errors
throw new Error('Something went wrong');
```

## Performance

### SolidJS is Fast by Default

- Don't optimize prematurely
- SolidJS only updates what changes
- Use `createMemo` for expensive computations only

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Memoize expensive filtering/sorting
const sortedItems = createMemo(() => 
  items().sort((a, b) => a.date - b.date)
);

// ❌ Bad: Don't memoize simple accessors
const itemName = createMemo(() => item().name);
```

## Testing

- Write tests for utility functions
- Write tests for complex data transformations
- Use Playwright MCP for UI testing
- Test error cases and edge cases

```typescript
// Example test structure
describe('formatDate', () => {
  it('formats recent dates as minutes', () => {
    const result = formatDate(Date.now() - 60000);
    expect(result).toBe('1m ago');
  });
});
```

## Monorepo Best Practices

### Package Dependencies

- Shared packages should have minimal dependencies
- Apps can depend on multiple shared packages
- Shared packages should not depend on apps

```json
// ✅ Good: App depends on shared packages
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@soundscape/types": "workspace:*",
    "@soundscape/utils": "workspace:*"
  }
}
```

### Building & Caching

- Always build shared packages before apps
- Turborepo handles this automatically
- Use `pnpm --filter` for targeted development

```bash
# ✅ Good: Let Turborepo handle dependencies
pnpm build

# ✅ Good: Develop specific package
pnpm --filter @soundscape/web dev
```

## Git Commit Messages

```bash
# ✅ Good: Descriptive commits with context
feat: add expandable tracks in albums view
fix: resolve LastFM API pagination issue
refactor: simplify track grouping logic
docs: update AGENTS.md with new patterns

# ❌ Bad: Vague commits
update files
fix bug
wip
```

## Documentation

- Update `AGENTS.md` when adding new patterns
- Add JSDoc comments for complex utility functions
- Document non-obvious behavior inline
- Keep README.md up to date

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Document complex logic
/**
 * Groups tracks by album, preserving the most recent play time.
 * Tracks without album info are grouped under an empty string key.
 */
export function groupTracksByAlbum(tracks: Track[]): RecentAlbum[] {
  // ...
}
```

## What to Avoid

- ❌ Over-engineering simple solutions
- ❌ Adding dependencies without careful consideration
- ❌ Breaking reactivity by destructuring props
- ❌ Using `any` type
- ❌ Inline styles (use Tailwind)
- ❌ Large components (split into smaller ones)
- ❌ Premature optimization
- ❌ Magic numbers (use named constants)
- ❌ Nested ternaries (use `<Show>` and `<Switch>`)

## When to Refactor

- When you find yourself copying code
- When a component exceeds ~150 lines
- When a function has more than 3 parameters
- When logic becomes hard to understand
- When tests become difficult to write

## Final Reminders

1. **Simplicity over cleverness** - Write obvious code
2. **Type everything** - Types are documentation
3. **Follow SolidJS patterns** - Don't fight the framework
4. **Design system first** - Use tokens, not arbitrary values
5. **Test edge cases** - Empty states, errors, loading states
6. **Read AGENTS.md** - Comprehensive project documentation

